{"id": "unknown-2026-08-06-009", "date": "2026-08-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["grid_parity", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Researchers compare PV, wind, hybrid systems for community-scale energy", "content": "<p>Researchers in China found a hybrid system combining 200 kW of PV, 200 kW of wind and a 100 kWh battery achieved a 70.8% self-sufficiency rate for a community consuming 1,000 kWh per day. While standalone PV delivered a lower levelized cost of energy, the hybrid configuration offered the best overall balance between cost and supply reliability.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/06/researchers-compare-pv-wind-hybrid-systems-for-community-scale-energy/\">Researchers co", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/06/researchers-compare-pv-wind-hybrid-systems-for-community-scale-energy/", "type": "rss"}]}
